<title>BELGIUM: PixTech FY 1996 loss widens.</title>
<headline>PixTech FY 1996 loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(all figures in millions of dollars, unless stated):</p>
<p>				 Q4 1996	 Q3 1996	  Q4 1995</p>
<p>    Net profit/loss     4.32 loss vs  4.56 loss  vs  1.58 profit</p>
<p>Net per share(dollars)$0.53 loss vs $0.56 loss  vs $0.20 profit</p>
<p>Twelve months ended Dec 31, 1996 (in millions of dollars,</p>
<p>unless stated):</p>
<p>    Net profit/loss	   11.72 loss  vs   6.30 loss</p>
<p>Net per share (dollars) $1.44 loss  vs  $0.82 loss</p>
<p>    No. shares outstanding   8.138 million  vs   7.697 million</p>
<p>NOTE - PixTech Inc is a manufacturer of flat-panel displays designed to replace liquid crystal displays (LCDs). It is listed on both the Nasdaq and Easdaq small cap markets.  </p>
<p>In a statement, PixTech said revenues in its fiscal year ending December 31, 1996 were $7.6 million compared with $11.5 million in 1995. Fourth quarter revenues amounted to $1.0 million, compared with $5.9 million in the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
